From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump follow-redirects and serialize-javascript for CVE-2026-116689 and CVE-2026-115897

Upstream: https://github.com/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/commit/b0a7751e9cd64cd8eeb6ec67d2f206a9cc88d3f8
Upstream: https://github.com/yahoo/serialize-javascript/commit/2864b3c6260a3bfd52d2db3e70d1a079de108a61

CVE-2026-116689: follow-redirects 1.16.1 -> 1.16.2. The sensitiveHeaders
option used instanceof Array instead of Array.isArray, so an array created
in another JavaScript realm was silently replaced with an empty list. A
cross-origin redirect could then forward a credential header named in that
discarded list to the redirect destination.

CVE-2026-115897: serialize-javascript 7.1.2 -> 7.1.4. The escapeFunctionBody
regex did not neutralize a bare </script prefix when it appeared at the very
end of a function body, allowing a spoofed toString() to break out of an HTML
script element.

diff --git a/package.json b/package.json
index e0ce95fc9af9..770d7a143f31 100644
--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -471,7 +471,9 @@
     "ip-address@npm:10.1.0": "10.3.1",
     "ip-address@npm:^9.0.5": "10.3.1",
     "body-parser@npm:^2.2.1": "2.4.0",
-    "body-parser@npm:1.20.3": "1.20.9"
+    "body-parser@npm:1.20.3": "1.20.9",
+    "follow-redirects": "1.16.2",
+    "serialize-javascript@npm:^7.0.3": "7.1.4"
   },
   "workspaces": {
     "packages": [
